{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193370-w20-rules-question-defense","id":1193370,"title":"W20 Rules Question: Defense","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-08T17:42:33-08:00","id":1193370,"title":"W20 Rules Question: Defense","content":"So on pg. 288, 289 it states: <i>&quot;A character who doesn\u2019t want to get hit with an attack has three options. Each one can be declared at any time before the opponent\u2019s attack, as long as a character has an action left to perform.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Meaning: if he/she doesn't have any dice pools left, and/or actions, they are screwed and can't use one of the defensive actions? It is an action yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13336-flash","name":"Flash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:33:09-08:00","id":1193387,"title":"","content":"Yep. You need an action (either normal declared or Rage) to defend yourself. You can abort to defense by sacrificing a different action, but you still need to have one.<br /> <br /> If you declared three attacks and didn't spend Rage for extra actions, roll all your attacks, and someone attacks you after... you're stuck taking the hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg"